# smoke.txtar — minimal sanity for the testscript harness itself.
#
# Exercises both custom commands against the STORY-0003 stub `nesdit`:
#   - `nesdit` runs and exits 0 with empty stdout
#   - `nesdit-idempotent` runs nesdit twice and asserts byte-identical stdout
#   - `fake-editor` rewrites a file from a scripted replacement
#
# Real feature fixtures land with STORY-0003+. This file exists to keep
# `make test-e2e` green from day one.

# 1. Bare nesdit exits 0.
nesdit
! stderr .

# 2. Idempotency harness is callable; stub returns identical (empty) stdout.
nesdit-idempotent help

# 3. fake-editor: no replacement configured -> target unchanged.
cp before.txt target.txt
fake-editor target.txt
cmp target.txt before.txt

# 4. fake-editor: replacement configured -> target overwritten.
env FAKE_EDITOR_REPLACE=after.txt
fake-editor target.txt
cmp target.txt after.txt

-- before.txt --
original contents
-- after.txt --
edited contents
-- target.txt --
placeholder — cp overwrites before each assertion
